Analysis of the data
Throughout my past four years at American University, I have engaged in discourse with students pursuing a variety of undergraduate and graduate degrees. In these discussions, I have often heard of many coding terms and libraries such as "R". However, this is language that I have not heard of in my journalism courses thus far. 
This data set, specifically in the pivot table bar chart shows how many students in the course who are also studying journalism, also do not have much knowledge on "R" or the panda libraries in python. While there are few students with ranging knowledge on the subject, a majority of students answered 0 for use of these coding libraries (if that is the correct terminology). This demonstrates (possibly) how beneficial this course will be in gaining a better knowledge and/or skills on these topics as the course moves throughout the semester.
